SM(374,{"n":"Numbers 26","a":"Fr Stephen De Young Archives/Numbers 26.mp3","d":2090.4,"s":[[0.4,"Come and study the Holy Scriptures with us as Father Stephen DeYoung teaches verse by verse on the podcast The Whole Counsel of God."],[9.12,"Father Stephen holds a PhD in Biblical Studies, and is an Orthodox priest serving at Archangel Gabriel Orthodox Church in Lafayette, Louisiana."],[25.84,"Chapter 26. Now it came to pass after the plague that the Lord spoke to Moses and Eliezer, the son of Aaron the priest, saying, Take a census of all the congregation of the sons of Israel from twenty years old and above by their father's houses, all able to go to war in Israel."],[47.12,"Anybody having deja vu flashbacks?"],[49.52,"I know it's been a while."],[50.48,"Some of you weren't here."],[52.24,"But back at the beginning of the Book of Numbers, we had a census."],[56.32,"Remember? All the tribes."],[58.56,"And I said, There's gonna be another census when we get toward the end."],[59.52,"another census. There's"],[62.04,"Here we are."],[65.32,"Why do we need another census?"],[66.92,"Well, remember, 40 years has passed between these census?"],[71.64,"Census? Census census?"],[73.96,"Anyway. Has passed."],[77.26,"So we had the first census was the generation that came out of Egypt."],[84.06,"And then remember, they all had to die off in the wilderness because of their faithlessness."],[91.04,"And then it's their children's generation, 40 years later, who are going to get to go into the land of Canaan."],[96.88,"And right now, here we're toward the end of the book."],[99.12,"We're getting ready to go in the land of Canaan."],[101.2,"So we're doing a census now of the new generation."],[103.04,"of And why is it the men that certain age?"],[105.41,"Of this generation."],[110.29,"Remember, as we've talked about, we are long before the period where anybody has a standing army."],[117.35,"You don't have standing armies."],[119.27,"They're really hard to feed."],[122.15,"Really hard to."],[123.51,"And so if you're a superpower at this point in the world, like Egypt, then you have people who are military commanders and generals and that kind of thing, who are sort of war advisors to the Pharaoh, who that's their whole job."],[139.75,"But in terms of your fighting forces, you just call up all the men, uh able-bodied men of a certain age before you go to war."],[147.67,"We've actually we actually saw this a couple times in Genesis where it talked about the time coming for war"],[147.69,"So you say, and there were certain periods of the year."],[155.13,"There'll be more of that later."],[156.25,"You're like, wait, the season for war."],[157.77,"What are you?"],[158.65,"And that was because you're calling up all the farmers."],[162.81,"You're calling up all the farm labor."],[165.45,"So you didn't go to war during the planting season or the harvest season."],[172.33,"Because you needed those people."],[173.61,"You had to feed your nation."],[175.63,"So you needed the labor there."],[177.47,"So they go to war after the harvest was done."],[181.31,"Because then you have several months before planting begins."],[185.39,"You can go and take all those people, call them out, make war, do whatever you're gonna do, take whatever territory you're gonna take, and then send them back for planting."],[194.47,"So, as weird as it sounds, and it's not that people cooperated, it's just you'd be destroying your own country."],[201.45,"People would starve."],[203.45,"Because none of the crops would get harvested if you tried to go to war in in some other time of year."],[208.66,"Like everybody kind of had to."],[211.14,"So there was just a season where wars happened."],[214.04,"Every year. If they were gonna happen, they happened."],[216.28,"It's like hurricane season."],[217.82,"We've got to be on lookout for hurricane, they had to be on lookout for foreign invasions."],[220.96,"Because they might try and come and take some territory."],[223.36,"But yeah, so and if you're talking about Israel, you don't have those generals and commanders, even."],[228.86,"You don't have those structures in place."],[230.54,"So it's purely all the men of that age gonna get called up."],[234.38,"We've talked before about how the fact the fact that they don't even really have weapons, uh the way we think of them, that they would were literally mostly using farm implements."],[246.98,"Or things that could be easily made."],[249.15,"You could take a long stick and sharpen the edge and call it a spear."],[252.61,"Like there are things that are pretty easily made."],[255.73,"Um but most of them are using what are called sickle swords, where they would take sickles used for farming and just kind of bang them out and straighten them a little."],[265.57,"That's where the whole thing in Isaiah comes from, where it talks about people beating their swords into plowshares, is how it's translated in English famously."],[275.33,"But the idea is they're just gonna turn them all back into farming implements because we're not gonna make war anymore."],[281.37,"At this time, we're probably it's going the other way."],[283.79,"You're getting called up."],[285.71,"You don't have any armor, you don't have any weapons, so just whatever you have."],[289.49,"You try and make a weapon out of it, because how well you do with that will determine whether you come home."],[295.81,"And this is why war at this time in history is pretty ugly and horrific."],[300.37,"It's just a bunch of men all piled on top of each other trying to beat each other to death, essentially, with crude implements until they break."],[311.01,"But what are the survival rates?"],[312.77,"Like, I've heard stuff that like relatively like it's not as bad like modern warfare, obviously."],[318.69,"But well, be so sort of because of that, you you didn't get the same kind of injuries."],[326.31,"Like, if you're hitting each other with clubs."],[329.53,"Like a lot of people are gonna come back with concussions and you know, and some people are gonna get killed."],[335.37,"And some people are gonna get broken limbs that never heal right, and that kind of thing."],[340.09,"But you're not getting limbs blown off, you're not getting the same kind of casualty level until you start getting some more military innovation."],[350.33,"The Assyrians, and then even more each step is more so."],[353.63,"Alexander the Great."],[354.91,"Once you get to the Romans, the Romans have basically a war machine, and they are just literally going and massacring whole villages of people and stuff."],[361.87,"But even then, they're doing it with like swords."],[364.91,"It's like up close and personal hacking people to pieces."],[366.35,"al. It's uh still super brut"],[371.43,"But yeah, these these wars had lower casualty rates from that."],[377.43,"Actually, a lot of the casualties in these kind of wars happen due to things like disease."],[383.05,"And malnutrition and stuff along the way."],[386.41,"Because you got huge groups of people hiking on foot to get places and then to get back and going to foreign areas."],[392.97,"So you you had a lot of disease and infection and and things like that."],[397.53,"And you had a lot of people who had just ended up debilitated."],[401.05,"They had a bad, you know, that because their arm would never heal right, or their shoulder, or their leg."],[406.49,"And there was no, they didn't have the sort of medical science to deal with that."],[411.05,"You were just debilitated"],[414.53,"But so uh that's why the census is of that."],[417.67,"Because they're getting ready to go into Canaan and they know there's gonna be a there's gonna be some fights coming."],[425.27,"Spoilers for the book of Joshua."],[427.12,"Uh they've already had a couple that we've seen, but there's gonna be some big fights coming, and so we're gonna now number the new generation."],[434.72,"So get ready for the raw excitement."],[438.24,"If you remember back when we did the first census and I read it, the beauty of repetition and rhythm."],[445.04,"Here it comes again."],[446.32,"So Moses and Eliezer the priest spoke with them in the arrowboat of Moab by the Jordan across from Jericho, saying, take a. census from twenty years old and above, in the manner of the Lord commanded Moses"],[459.56,"Now the sons of Israel who came out of Egypt were Reuben, the firstborn of Israel."],[465.56,"The sons of Reuben were Enoch and the tribe of the Enochites, Paliu and the tribe of the Pali Peliuites, Hezron and the tribe of the Hezronites, Carmi and the tribe of the Carmelite, Carmiites."],[479.72,"These are the tribes of Reuben, and their census was forty-three thousand seven hundred and thirty."],[486.28,"Now the son of Paliu was Eliab."],[488.84,"The sons of Eliab were Nemuel, Dathan, and Abiram."],[493.0,"These were the ones chosen by the congregation to form a coalition against Moses and Aaron in the company of Korah in their revolt against the Lord, and the earth opened its mouth, swallowed them and Korah in the death of his company, when fire devoured two hundred and fifty men, and they became a sign, but the sons of Korah did not die."],[513.04,"Okay, so that's a little bit of history."],[514.96,"We already read that story."],[516.58,"And about that some of the sons of Korah survived."],[520.1,"They'll show up again when we get to the book of Psalms here in a couple of years."],[524.5,"We will revisit them then."],[526.18,"But so remember when it's talking about sons, it's not being literal in the sense that like Reuben was not alive when they came out of Egypt, nor were his sons, nor were his grandchildren."],[541.3,"They were in Egypt for several centuries."],[544.1,"So this is talking about so Reuben is the tribe, like the big tribe"],[550.7,"And then the people described as the sons of Reuben, those are the clans."],[555.9,"Those are the big clans."],[557.82,"And the names are the clan heads."],[561.1,"And then the sons of those clan names are the big extended families within those clans."],[570.14,"And then there's all the people, within each of those units."],[574.24,"So you've got big extended families, groups of those make up clans, groups of those clans make up the tribes."],[583.52,"That's how this is structured."],[586.0,"And there's gonna be 12 of these because Manasseh and Ephraim are both from Joseph, but Levi doesn't get counted for this because the Levites are priests and don't do military service."],[596.94,"If you remember from last time."],[598.94,"The other note, before we get into the fun, repetitious reading, is that remember, we're getting these thousands of people, and it seems like these huge numbers, and you may be thinking, like, that's literally impossible for a camp that size to be like moving through the wilderness and stuff, the desert."],[615.02,"And you are correct, these numbers are not exact."],[618.94,"So thousand is used just to mean big number or company."],[626.78,"Uh it does not literally mean 1,000 people."],[631.66,"Thousand means big group."],[633.42,"Okay And this is true not just in the ancient Near East, this is true throughout the ancient world."],[638.82,"The Roman military, a centurion, was in charge of how many people?"],[644.74,"Anyone know? 82."],[646.9,"Yes, that is actually correct."],[648.5,"82. You say century, well, that's a hundred."],[652.18,"It's a hundred men."],[653.38,"And that you will see that in the Roman records."],[656.18,"He was in charge of a hundred."],[658.02,"But a hundred was actually 82 people."],[661.38,"It was just rounded off."],[662.9,"On paper, it looks good."],[664.2,"It was just rounded off."],[665.72,"So these are rounded off numbers."],[669.0,"So what it actually says is, 43,730 is 43,000. 7s, and then 3"],[682.36,"But those thousands may have been eight hundred and ninety-two people, those hundreds may have been eighty-two people, or a hundred and two people, and thirty was probably about thirty."],[696.14,"But so this isn't uh super strictly accurate."],[702.0,"Numbering. Okay. Verse twelve."],[706.16,"The sons of Sibion and the tribe of the sons of Simeon were Nemuel and the tribe of the Nemulites, and Jammon and the tribe of the Jaminites, and Jacan and the tribe of the Jaconites, and Zerah and the and tri thebe tribe of the Zarites, and Shaul of the Shaolites."],[721.68,"of the These are the tribes Simeonites, and their census was 22,200."],[734.44,"All the same things I just said still apply."],[737.8,"So now I'm going to move quickly."],[746.92,"After these, Judah's sons, according to their tribes."],[750.54,"So those are here, Er and Onan, remember, are actual people."],[754.38,"We read about them in Genesis."],[756.06,"Those two people died."],[757.34,"And so what this is telling us is there was no later tribe named after them because they didn't have any descendants."],[765.84,"So there's no tribe or clan or anything related to them."],[770.2,"After these, so after these, meaning the ones who did have clans."],[777.0,"After these, Judah's sons, according to their tribes, were Shelah and the tribe of the Shelaites, and Perez and the tribe of the Perazites, and Zerah, the tribe of the Zeraites."],[788.92,"Now the sons of Peres were Hezron and the tribe of the Hezronites, and Hamul and the tribe of the Hamulites."],[796.04,"These are the tribes of Judah, according to their census, 76,500."],[801.16,"The sons of Issachar, according to their tribes, were Tola and the tribe of the Tolaites, and Puah and the tribe of the Pu'ites, and Jashub and the tribe of the Jashabites, and and Shimron the tribe of the Shimronites, these are the tribes of Issachar from their census, sixty-four thousand three hundred."],[819.68,"And we just keep rolling on."],[821.36,"Sons of Zebulun according to their tribes were Sared and the tribe of the Sarodites and Elon, not the one you're thinking of, and the tribe of the Elonites, and Jalel and the tribe of the Jalelites, these are the tribes of Zebulun from their census, sixty thousand five hundred."],[840.0,"The sons of Gad according to their tribes were Zephon and the tribe of the Zephonites, and Hagi and the tribe of the Hagiites, and Shuni and the tribe of the Shunites, and Ozni and the tribe of the Ozniites, and Adi and the tribe of the Adiititeses, and, and Erod and the tribe of the Erid and Areli the tribe of the Arelites."],[861.96,"These are the tribes of the sons of Gad from their census, 40,500."],[867.32,"Sons of Asher, according to their tribes, were Jimnah and the tribe of the Jimnaites, Jesul and the tribe of the Jesuites, and Bariah and the tribe of the Bereaites, and Heber and the tribe of the Heborites, and Malchiel and the tribe of the Malchelites."],[885.32,"Now the name of Asher's daughter was Sarah."],[891.16,"So she doesn't have a tribe or a clan named after her."],[894.2,"But the reason she's mentioned is not just like, oh hey, by the way, he also had a daughter."],[899.32,"It's that there are people descended from her, who are considered part of the tribe, even though they're not part of one of the clans just mentioned."],[913.28,"So there are some other folks."],[921.88,"The sons of Joseph, according to their tribes, were Manasseh and Ephraim."],[926.12,"The son of Manasseh was Makir and the tribe of the Makirites."],[930.84,"And Makir begot Gilead, and by Gilead the tribe of the Gileadites."],[936.12,"Now these are the sons of Gilead, Je Jeszerus, and the tribe of the Jezerites, and Helech and the family of the Helekites, and Asrael and the tribe of the Asraelites, and Shechem and the tribe of the Shechemites, and Shemitah and the tribe of the Shemedaites, and Hepher and the tribe of the Heferites."],[956.88,"Now Zalopahad, the son of Hefer, had no sons but daughters, and the names of the daughters of Zalopahad were Mala, Noah, Hogla, Milka, and Tirzah."],[968.48,"These are the tribes of Manasseh from their census, 52,700."],[972.4,"So same thing with the daughters there."],[974.4,"All of these are great biblical names."],[977.04,"If you're looking for, yeah, if you want to name your kid Jeezer, I do not I do not recommend naming your daughter Hogla."],[985.28,"She will grow up to murder you if you name her Hogla."],[989.44,"Also not a great thing to name your daughter"],[989.8,"Heifer's not good."],[990.92,"Yeah, Heifer, also not great."],[995.4,"So I might, if you come to me with that at a baptism, I might change it on you just for your sake."],[1001.32,"But some of I mean Jesus, come on."],[1004.36,"Yeah. Verse 39."],[1006.36,"Now these are the sons of Ephraim, Shuthala and the tribe of the Shuthalites, Shuthalaites, and Tehan and the tribe of the Tehanites."],[1016.6,"Now these are the sons of Shufala, Iran and the tribe of the Aaronites."],[1022.28,"These are the tribes of the sons of Ephraim from their census 32,500."],[1025.72,"These tribes are the sons of Joseph according to their tribes"],[1031.64,"The sons of Benjamin according to their tribes were Bela and the tribe of the Belaites, and Ashbel and the tribe of the Ashbelites, and Ahiram and the family of the Ahiramites, and Shufim and the tribe of the Shufhamites."],[1047.36,"Now the sons of Bela were Ard and Naaman, Ard and the tribe of the Ardites, and Naaman and the tribe of the Naamanites."],[1054.72,"These are the sons of Benjamin according to their tribes from their census, forty-five thousand six hundred."],[1060.96,"This is the son of Dan according to his tribe, Shuhan and the tribe of the Shuhnites, Shuhamites."],[1067.44,"This is the tribe of Dan according to Shuhem's tribe."],[1070.32,"The entire tribe of the Shufimites, from their census, was sixty-four thousand four hundred."],[1075.52,"So this is one of the interesting things about Dan."],[1077.68,"You may have heard me say before: the Danit.es are mostly not even Semitic"],[1083.64,"The Danites are actually one of the sea peoples who kind of get adopted into Israel."],[1089.0,"And there's several ways that this is telegraphed."],[1091.4,"You may be wondering why are they after Benjamin?"],[1101.24,"Well, because according to Genesis, Dan, like some of these other tribes that we're about to read, were his children through concubines, not through his wives."],[1112.78,"So there's already kind of a tip-off in Genesis that Dan is not, shall we say, a legitimate son."],[1119.92,"Of Jacob. We also have this thing here, notice where there's only one clan."],[1124.48,"Tribe of Dan is made up of one clan"],[1131.4,"Just one big clan."],[1133.08,"And that's another tip-off that this is a group who's been kind of, for the most part, adopted, adopted in."],[1140.52,"There are lots of individuals who we've seen and will continue to see were adopted in."],[1145.5,"But this is a whole group that's been adopted in, and there's these various tip-offs."],[1151.1,"And we're going to learn a lot of other bad things about Dan as we go."],[1155.1,"They're never going to be very good Israelites."],[1157.46,"Uh they're going to continue with a lot of their pagan sea peoples."],[1160.62,"By sea peoples, I mean they're Greek."],[1164.7,"Well, in this case, they're this they're the people who Homer calls the Danae, they're the same group, yeah"],[1172.66,"They also have one of the biggest um kidding the biggest numbers, yeah, of military age people, yeah, yeah."],[1182.5,"Gee, why would a group of sea people have a large military populace?"],[1189.16,"Because they're mainly a military unit, and that's probably part of how they were adopted in, is because the sea peoples who came, it's not like families migrating, they came and attacked Egypt."],[1201.28,"And then ended up settling along the coast of the Lofant, like the Philistines, and so they needed wives to be blood."],[1212.33,"They probably had a few women with them, but like this is mostly men."],[1213.13,"So they would have intermarried with local people"],[1216.21,"This is mostly military."],[1220.43,"And so that's probably part of how this sort of adoption took place."],[1225.81,"Uh it and again, the concept of ethnicity is a new one."],[1230.95,"So it didn't matter that Phineas and a Danite looked like really different physically."],[1237.33,"That wasn't the issue."],[1239.33,"They didn't have our concept of ethnicity."],[1241.81,"Levi wasn't. Yeah, we skipped Levi."],[1245.57,"Yeah. Levi should have been between Simeon and Judah in terms of birth order, but was skipped because they don't do military service."],[1254.77,"Back to it"],[1257.45,"Sons of Naphtali, according to their tribes, were Jezeel and the tribe of the Jezeelites, and Guni and the tribe of the Guniites."],[1266.17,"Wouldn't it be great to be a Guniite?"],[1268.65,"You probably also should not name your son Guni."],[1271.77,"That would probably not go well for him."],[1273.61,"And Jezer and the tribe of the Jezreites and Shilim and the family of the Shilamites, these are the tribes of Naphtali and their census, 45,400."],[1284.41,"This is the census of the sons of Israel, 601,730."],[1291.69,"Yes, so 600,000, you're going, wait, what?"],[1295.13,"It's not an error."],[1296.17,"Again, we talked about round numbers."],[1298.7,"That's then the Lord spoke to Moses, saying, To these the land shall be divided as an inheritance based on the number of names."],[1306.74,"To a large tribe you shall give a larger inheritance, and to a small tribe you shall give a smaller inheritance."],[1311.78,"Each shall be given its inheritance based on its census, but the land shall be divided by lot."],[1316.18,"They shall inherit according to the names of the tribes of their fathers."],[1319.7,"By allotment, their inheritance shall be divided between them larger and smaller."],[1324.34,"So this is the main purpose of this."],[1331.18,"Is the idea that based on the number of people, each person, basically each family, is going to get the same size plot of land that's going to be theirs."],[1344.88,"It's going to belong to their family from God."],[1347.6,"That little piece to that family."],[1350.08,"And where that is, that's the decided by lot part."],[1355.2,"And that's to make it quote unquote fair."],[1357.74,"Somebody's like, man, my land's, you know, like desert."],[1360.23,"My land, like his land's better than my land."],[1362.65,"So that's right, we're gonna do a fair way of deciding it."],[1366.49,"That's gonna belong to that family, and then this is gonna be the basis for the year of Jubilee."],[1371.87,"That supposedly, and they never do this, but we already read of it."],[1375.35,"Supposedly, they were supposed to, in the 50th year, all the land would go back to the families that originally had it."],[1383.97,"So if you were a really good businessman and a wheeler dealer and you, your neighbor was not so smart or bright or was lazy or whatever, might end up owning half his land."],[1395.13,"But that wouldn't last forever."],[1397.29,"When the 50th year came up, it would go back there where it was."],[1401.61,"So your son and his son would start out on the same level."],[1406.09,"So this was to make sure that there would be no generational poverty."],[1410.73,"So if you were lazy or not very bright or just made really bad decisions, you might suffer for it."],[1418.87,"And your immediate family might suffer for it for a period of time while you were the head of the family, but then that you would not then pass on that poverty to the next generation."],[1430.23,"They would get a new start, they could make better decisions, they could work more diligently."],[1434.77,"They could they could do better."],[1436.77,"That was God's intent."],[1438.13,"That's the system God sets up in the Torah."],[1441.09,"As we know, that's not how things work out."],[1444.34,"But this was entirely equal based on number."],[1447.62,"Everyone got the same start, but everyone they also were just given the land."],[1453.46,"They had to plant, they had to harvest, they had right, so they have to do the work and invest the time and the work and the effort into that."],[1462.26,"But they all started out in each generation, would have if they had followed what God set out."],[1468.5,"An equal plane, they all get an equal share."],[1471.54,"So that's that's the real reason why we needed this census."],[1475.06,"God's already covered that, he's gonna fight for them"],[1476.08,"It's not like, oh, we don't have enough people, we're not gonna be able to win the war."],[1481.74,"They could bring five guys and they'd still win."],[1484.34,"Like the point is we're gonna give every family right their equal share, their equal starting point."],[1490.42,"And we're gonna see, by the way, that according to the Torah, this isn't just true of Israel."],[1499.3,"This is true of everybody on earth."],[1501.62,"Well, when we get into the beginning of Deuteronomy, we're gonna see that with Israel's neighbors."],[1506.1,"But the idea is that, and St."],[1508.74,"Paul's gonna appeal to this in Acts 17, that God actually gives each nation and each person in each nation."],[1515.32,"That every human essentially, God gives a a share, is entitled to share of what God has created."],[1522.16,"They could squander that and they could be lazy, they could, etc."],[1524.72,"etc. They could suffer the consequences of that."],[1526.96,"But it's God's intent that that not be a generational thing."],[1531.28,"Period. That everyone have an equal right opportunity."],[1536.5,"And then, of course, then it's up to you."],[1539.16,"What you do with it, with what God has given you."],[1542.7,"And then what you do with God has given you should determine what goes forward."],[1548.3,"And as we've said before, Israel strays super far from this."],[1552.54,"They never do the Sabbath year, let alone the Jubilee."],[1555.74,"Never happens. And as we said before, in the New Testament, when we're in the New Testament, by the time you get to Christ's ministry, uh, the high priest's family and the other Sadducees own 70% of the land in Judea that isn't owned by the Romans."],[1575.07,"That anyone owns."],[1576.11,"70% of it is owned by another big chunk is Herod."],[1579.69,"But it's not owned by any of the people."],[1582.81,"And that the high priest family had done that on purpose, that they had used the temple tax to indebt the people and then seize their land and essentially employ them at low wages to work the land that God had given them in the first place to be their own."],[1601.95,"So even in Israel, at Judea, this doesn't, let alone other nations."],[1605.31,"It doesn't even approximate what God intended"],[1612.95,"But that is seen by the Torah as a basic injustice when that happens."],[1618.55,"Now the sons of Levi, so now we get to Levi."],[1621.21,"Because we're we're we're done with that."],[1622.83,"The Levites also remember are not going to get land because they're going to be surrounding the tabernacle and then later the temple."],[1631.07,"They're going to be living there."],[1632.43,"They're not going to be farming."],[1633.63,"They're going to be serving as priests and doing these things that they're going to eat from the offerings that get brought by everyone else."],[1639.87,"That's where they're going to get their food and upkeep."],[1644.43,"Now, the sons of Levi, according to their tribes, were Gershon and the tribe of the Gershonites, and and Ko Kohathath.h the tribe of theites, and Marari and the tribe of the Merariites"],[1655.51,"These are the tribes of the sons of Levi, the tribe of the Libniites, the tribe of the Hebronites, the tribe of the Koraites, and the tribe of the Mushites."],[1667.43,"You only see LC Mushi."],[1670.15,"Mushi would be a great."],[1672.23,"Now Kohat begot Amram."],[1675.27,"The name of Amram's wife was Yacobed, the daughter of Levi, who was born to Levi in Egypt."],[1681.59,"And to Amram she bore Aaron and Moses and their sister Miriam."],[1685.91,"So that's where Moses fits in in terms of the tribes and clans of Levi."],[1691.67,"To Aaron were born Nadab and Abahu, Eliezer and Ithamar."],[1694.47,"and But Nadab Abuhu died when they offered strange fire before the Lord in the Sinai Desert."],[1699.95,"Now, based on their census, they numbered twenty-three thousand, every male from a month old and above."],[1706.99,"For a census was not taken of them among the other sons of Israel, because there was no allotment given to them among the sons of Israel."],[1714.19,"They don't serve in the military, they don't get a land allotment."],[1716.91,"So they counted, so military age is irrelevant."],[1720.52,"So they just count all the males, period."],[1724.36,"This is the census of Moses and Eliezer the priest, who numbered the sons of Israel in Erebot of Moab by the Jordan across from Jericho."],[1733.24,"But among these there was not a man numbered by Moses and Aaron the priest when they took a census of the of the sons Israel in Sinai Desert."],[1741.76,"Meaning, those guys who they counted before are all gone."],[1746.34,"And now, does that mean every single human?"],[1751.14,"No. No, not just that."],[1753.22,"Remember, military age."],[1755.94,"So some of these people were alive at that time, but they were kids."],[1759.72,"And feasibly there might be a few, like Moses himself, there might be a few very elderly people banging around."],[1766.22,"Still at this point in time, who were counted last time."],[1769.92,"But they're not counted this time because they're too old now."],[1773.49,"They're not going to be around too much longer."],[1776.61,"For the Lord said to them, they shall surely die in the desert."],[1779.89,"So there was not left a man of them except Caleb the son of Jephuna and Joshua the son of Nun."],[1785.71,"Remember, they are the two spies who were faithful."],[1789.55,"And just while we're on the whole ethnic diversity thing, remember that Caleb is not only a Canaanite, uh, he's a Kennesite."],[1800.59,"He's from one of the groups that Israel's going to destroy."],[1804.03,"One of the groups that Israel's going to wipe out."],[1805.87,"But guess what?"],[1806.51,"They're not going to kill Caleb."],[1807.79,"Why are they not going to kill Caleb?"],[1809.47,"Because Caleb is now an elder of the tribe of Judah."],[1813.79,"He's not only joined, yes, he ceased being a Kennesite, he's now a member of the tribe of Judah."],[1819.47,"He is a son of Judah."],[1821.07,"He is, as far as they are concerned, descended from the person Judah."],[1825.17,"So this is why I say our modern concept of ethnicity is not here."],[1830.51,"And not only is he a member of the tribe of Judah and considered to be descended from Judah, he's an elder in the tribe of Judah."],[1837.07,"Meaning he's the head of one of the clans."],[1841.65,"His family is now part of the tribe of Judah."],[1845.17,"So he's literally considered one of the sons of Judah in this kind of numbering, even though he's no biological relation."],[1852.61,"Yeah. Does that kind of it kind of m meade think about the idea of being rafted in in, you know, like the new covenant?"],[1860.45,"Yeah. That kind of thing."],[1861.73,"Is the way you were talking about that and how they viewed it kind of reminded me, is that in some way connected?"],[1867.53,"the The way way it's yes, it's essentially the same."],[1870.05,"Yeah That the the when you look at the origin of Israel, so there is this meme in a lot of evangelical circles, and Protestant circles in general, which is that sometimes they even say salvation."],[1890.57,"Which is crazy to me, but at least the covenant or the people of God was quote-unquote ethnic in the old testament."],[1900.33,"And then in the new testament, well, now it's based on quote-unquote belief."],[1904.42,"Like that's their meme."],[1905.86,"And before we even get to the faith and belief part, which is what people usually argue about, it was never ethnic in the in the way we think of it."],[1918.42,"So, yes, there was a nation, Israel, that was a nation for a brief period of time."],[1923.88,"That it was actually called Israel."],[1925.24,"I mean, we're talking about a couple centuries, like America's been around longer."],[1928.74,"But but there was, you know, a continuous mass of people, but they were ethnically diverse."],[1935.03,"And especially here at the start, you see that."],[1938.25,"This is a group of people from all different ethnic backgrounds who are gathered together, and they're made sons of these patriarchal figures by being brought into the people, which is a ritual thing."],[1950.65,"They're the men are circumcised and they eat the Passover, so they're Israelites."],[1955.53,"That's what it takes to be an Israelite there's they don't know what DNA is right there's no biological thing they're not making family trees to decide if you're Jewish right it's you're circumcised you eat the you eat the Passover but it doesn't stop there we're gonna see all the way through right you know uh David's uh great grandma is a Moabite Ruth right all through there are gonna be people of different ethnic right who are who are brought in and who become part of yeah, Rahab's gonna be put become part of the tribe of Judah."],[1991.71,"And there's gonna be Deuteronomy's gonna lay out processes for that with women, because since women aren't circumcised."],[1998.21,"It's gonna lay out processes for women coming into Israel."],[2000.73,"What did they do ritually since they're not doing the circumcision part?"],[2004.61,"They do eat the Passover."],[2006.23,"Men, women, and children all eat the Passover, but children eat the Passover."],[2009.99,"Anyway, sorry. Yeah, you see what I did there."],[2014.55,"Um, but right, so there's there's processes for that, yeah."],[2018.15,"So I'm trying to emphasize that."],[2019.91,"And so um what happens with the church."],[2025.6,"So the the church is Israel, it's the same group."],[2029.06,"It's just there's another big grafting in that begins."],[2033.84,"But a big grafting in is how it all started, and little grafting ins have been continuous all the way through, so there's not really a disjunction there."],[2044.56,"Or m as much of one as certain groups and certain folks would like to see"],[2067.8,"Listen next time as Father Stephen DeYoung continues his study of the scriptures on the Whole Counsel of God."],[2075.16,"Father Stephen's email address is wholecounsel at ancientfaith.com."],[2080.44,"That's wholecounsel at ancientfaith.com."]],"o":[{"t":25.84,"lv":2,"h":"Numbers 26:1-4 - Census of the new generation","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>Numbers 26</b> - after the <b>plague</b>, Lord tells Moses + <b>Eliezer</b> the priest: census, <b>20 years and up</b>, all able to go to war</li><li class=\"d0\">\"Deja vu\" - <b>first census</b> at start of Numbers; said then there'd be <b>another near the end</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Why again? <b>40 years</b> have passed</li><li class=\"d1\">1st census = generation out of <b>Egypt</b></li><li class=\"d1\">they all <b>died off in the wilderness</b> for faithlessness</li><li class=\"d1\">now their <b>children</b> are the ones to enter <b>Canaan</b></li><li class=\"d0\">So: number the <b>new generation</b> before going in</li></ul>"},{"t":103.04,"lv":3,"h":"Why only men of fighting age","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">No <b>standing armies</b> this early - \"really hard to feed\"</li><li class=\"d1\">superpowers like <b>Egypt</b> had generals, war advisors to Pharaoh</li><li class=\"d1\">fighting force = <b>call up all able-bodied men</b> of age</li><li class=\"d0\">Seen in <b>Genesis</b> - \"the time coming for war\"</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Season for war</b> - calling up the <b>farm labor</b></li><li class=\"d1\">not during <b>planting or harvest</b> - you had to feed the nation</li><li class=\"d1\">go after harvest, <b>months before planting</b>, take territory, send men home</li><li class=\"d1\">war any other time = <b>destroy your own country</b>, people starve</li><li class=\"d0\">\"Like <b>hurricane season</b>\" - watch for foreign invasions</li><li class=\"d0\">Israel has <b>no generals or structures</b> at all - purely all the men of that age</li></ul>"},{"t":234.38,"lv":3,"h":"Weapons: sickle swords","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Don't really have <b>weapons</b> as we think of them - mostly <b>farm implements</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Or things easily made - sharpened long stick = <b>spear</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Sickle swords</b> - bang out farming sickles, straighten a little</li><li class=\"d1\">source of <b>Isaiah</b>: beat <b>swords into plowshares</b></li><li class=\"d1\">= turn them back into farm tools, \"we're not gonna make war anymore\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Now going the other way: no armor, no weapons, make one from whatever you have</li><li class=\"d0\">How well you do with it <b>determines whether you come home</b></li><li class=\"d0\">War then = \"pretty ugly and horrific\" - men piled on top of each other beating each other with <b>crude implements until they break</b></li></ul>"},{"t":311.01,"lv":3,"h":"How deadly was ancient war","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Q: survival rates?</li><li class=\"d0\">Not like modern warfare - clubs = <b>concussions</b>, some killed, <b>broken limbs that never heal</b></li><li class=\"d0\">But no limbs blown off - casualty level rises with <b>military innovation</b></li><li class=\"d1\"><b>Assyrians</b>, then each step more so, <b>Alexander the Great</b></li><li class=\"d1\"><b>Romans</b> = \"war machine\", massacre whole villages - still swords, \"up close and personal hacking\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Lower casualty rates in these wars</li><li class=\"d0\">Many casualties from <b>disease and malnutrition</b></li><li class=\"d1\">huge groups hiking on foot to foreign areas and back</li><li class=\"d1\">infection; people left <b>debilitated</b> - arm, shoulder, leg never healed right</li><li class=\"d1\">no medical science to deal with it</li></ul>"},{"t":414.53,"lv":3,"h":"Why the census: fights coming","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">That's why the census is of fighting men</li><li class=\"d0\">Getting ready to enter <b>Canaan</b> - <b>some fights coming</b></li><li class=\"d0\">\"Spoilers for the book of <b>Joshua</b>\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Already had a couple, but <b>big fights</b> ahead</li><li class=\"d0\">Number the <b>new generation</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Warning: raw excitement - \"the beauty of <b>repetition and rhythm</b>\", reads the list again</li></ul>"},{"t":434.72,"lv":2,"h":"Numbers 26:5-11 - Reuben and Korah's sons","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Moses + Eliezer speak to them in the <b>plains of Moab</b>, by the <b>Jordan</b> across from <b>Jericho</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Reuben</b>, firstborn - clans: <b>Enoch, Pallu, Hezron, Carmi</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Census of Reuben: <b>43,730</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Aside on <b>Pallu's line</b>: <b>Eliab</b> → <b>Dathan and Abiram</b></li><li class=\"d1\">the ones who formed a coalition against Moses + Aaron with <b>Korah</b></li><li class=\"d1\"><b>earth swallowed</b> them; <b>fire</b> devoured the 250 → \"a sign\"</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>But sons of Korah did not die</b></li><li class=\"d1\">\"a little bit of history\" - already read that story</li><li class=\"d1\">they'll show up again in the <b>Psalms</b> \"in a couple of years\"</li></ul>"},{"t":526.18,"lv":3,"h":"Sons, clans, tribes: how it's structured","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">\"Sons of Reuben\" not literal - Reuben not alive at the exodus, nor his sons/grandchildren</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>several centuries</b> in Egypt</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Reuben</b> = the tribe</li><li class=\"d0\">\"Sons of Reuben\" = the <b>big clans</b>; names are the <b>clan heads</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Their sons = <b>extended families</b> within the clans</li><li class=\"d0\">Then all the people within each unit</li><li class=\"d1\">families → <b>clans</b> → <b>tribes</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>12 tribes</b> still: <b>Manasseh + Ephraim</b> both from Joseph</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Levi not counted</b> - priests, no military service</li></ul>"},{"t":598.94,"lv":3,"h":"The numbers are rounded","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Thousands of people - \"literally impossible\" for a camp that size crossing the desert? <b>Correct - not exact</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Thousand</b> = \"big number or company\", <b>big group</b></li><li class=\"d1\">true across the ancient Near East and <b>whole ancient world</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Roman <b>centurion</b> - in charge of how many? <b>82</b> (audience got it)</li><li class=\"d1\">records say \"a hundred\"; really <b>82</b> - \"rounded off, on paper it looks good\"</li><li class=\"d0\">So <b>43,730</b> = 43 \"thousands\", 7 \"hundreds\", ~30</li><li class=\"d1\">the \"thousands\" might be <b>892</b> people; hundreds could be 82 or 102</li><li class=\"d1\">\"not super strictly accurate numbering\"</li></ul>"},{"t":702.0,"lv":2,"h":"Numbers 26:12-37 - Simeon to Manasseh","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>Simeon</b> (v.12) - Nemuel, Jamin, Jachin, Zerah, Shaul → <b>22,200</b></li><li class=\"d0\">\"All the same things I just said still apply\" - moving quickly</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Judah</b> - <b>Er and Onan</b> are real people, from <b>Genesis</b></li><li class=\"d1\">both <b>died</b>, no descendants → no tribe named after them</li><li class=\"d0\">Judah's clans: <b>Shelah, Perez, Zerah</b> (Perez → Hezron, Hamul) → <b>76,500</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Issachar</b> → <b>64,300</b>; <b>Zebulun</b> → <b>60,500</b> (\"<b>Elon</b>, not the one you're thinking of\")</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Gad</b> → <b>40,500</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Asher</b> - note his daughter <b>Serah</b></li><li class=\"d1\">not a clan, but mentioned because <b>people descended from her</b> count in the tribe</li><li class=\"d1\">\"some other folks\" outside the named clans</li></ul>"},{"t":921.88,"lv":3,"h":"Joseph's sons; Zelophehad's daughters","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>Manasseh</b> → <b>Machir</b> → <b>Gilead</b> and his sons (Jeezer, Helek, Asriel, Shechem, Shemida, Hepher)</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Zelophehad</b>, son of Hepher: <b>no sons, only daughters</b></li><li class=\"d1\"><b>Mahlah, Noah, Hoglah, Milcah, Tirzah</b></li><li class=\"d1\">same point as Asher's daughter</li><li class=\"d0\">Manasseh total: <b>52,700</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Names humor: \"great biblical names\" - but don't name your daughter <b>Hoglah</b> - \"she will grow up to murder you\"</li><li class=\"d1\">also not <b>Heifer</b></li><li class=\"d1\">\"if you come to me with that at a baptism, I might change it on you\"</li></ul>"},{"t":1004.36,"lv":2,"h":"Numbers 26:39-47 - Ephraim, Benjamin, Dan","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>Ephraim</b> (v.39) - Shuthelah, Becher, Tahan (Shuthelah → Eran) → <b>32,500</b></li><li class=\"d0\">\"These are the sons of <b>Joseph</b>\"</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Benjamin</b> - Bela, Ashbel, Ahiram, Shephupham; Bela → Ard, Naaman → <b>45,600</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Dan</b> - one son, <b>Shuham</b> → <b>64,400</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Interesting thing about Dan: <b>mostly not even Semitic</b></li><li class=\"d0\">One of the <b>sea peoples</b> adopted into Israel - several tip-offs</li><li class=\"d1\">placed <b>after Benjamin</b> - in <b>Genesis</b>, Dan and the next tribes were sons of <b>concubines</b>, not wives</li><li class=\"d1\">\"not, shall we say, a legitimate son of Jacob\"</li><li class=\"d1\">only <b>one clan</b> - a group adopted in</li></ul>"},{"t":1140.52,"lv":3,"h":"Dan: sea peoples and the military","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Individuals adopted in, seen all through - but Dan is a <b>whole group</b></li><li class=\"d0\">\"We're going to learn a lot of other <b>bad things about Dan</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\">\"never going to be very good Israelites\"; keep <b>pagan sea peoples</b> ways</li><li class=\"d0\">Sea peoples = <b>Greek</b> - Homer's <b>Danaans</b>, same group</li><li class=\"d0\">Among the <b>biggest numbers</b> of military-age men</li><li class=\"d1\">\"why would sea people have a large military populace?\" - mainly a <b>military unit</b></li><li class=\"d1\">sea peoples <b>attacked Egypt</b>, then settled the <b>Levant</b> coast like the <b>Philistines</b></li><li class=\"d1\">not families migrating - few women → <b>intermarried with locals</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Ethnicity</b> a modern concept - <b>Phinehas and a Danite</b> looking physically different wasn't the issue</li><li class=\"d0\">Levi skipped - belongs between <b>Simeon and Judah</b> in birth order, <b>no military service</b></li></ul>"},{"t":1254.77,"lv":2,"h":"Numbers 26:48-51 - Naphtali and the total","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>Naphtali</b> - Jahzeel, Guni, Jezer, Shillem → <b>45,400</b></li><li class=\"d0\">\"Wouldn't it be great to be a <b>Gunite</b>?\" - don't name your son Guni</li><li class=\"d0\">Total census of Israel: <b>601,730</b></li><li class=\"d0\">\"600,000, you're going, wait, what?\" - <b>not an error</b>, round numbers</li></ul>"},{"t":1298.7,"lv":2,"h":"Numbers 26:52-56 - Land by lot","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Lord: land divided <b>by number of names</b> - large tribe, larger inheritance; small tribe, smaller</li><li class=\"d0\">But divided <b>by lot</b>, by the names of their fathers' tribes</li><li class=\"d0\">\"The main purpose\" of the census</li><li class=\"d0\">Each <b>family</b> gets the <b>same size plot</b>, theirs <b>from God</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Lot = \"quote unquote <b>fair</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\">no one saying \"his land's better than my land\" - desert vs good land</li><li class=\"d0\">Basis for the <b>year of Jubilee</b></li></ul>"},{"t":1371.87,"lv":3,"h":"Jubilee: no generational poverty","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">\"They never do this, but we already read of it\" - <b>50th year</b>: land returns to the original families</li><li class=\"d0\">Sharp businessman could end up owning <b>half his neighbor's land</b></li><li class=\"d1\">wouldn't last: <b>Jubilee</b> sends it back</li><li class=\"d1\">\"your son and his son start out on the <b>same level</b>\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Purpose: <b>no generational poverty</b></li><li class=\"d1\">lazy or bad decisions → you and your immediate family may suffer</li><li class=\"d1\">but you <b>don't pass poverty on</b> - next generation gets a <b>new start</b></li><li class=\"d0\">God's intent - the system set up in the <b>Torah</b> - \"as we know, that's not how things work out\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Equal start, but must still <b>plant, harvest, do the work</b></li></ul>"},{"t":1471.54,"lv":3,"h":"Real reason for the census: equal share","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">\"The real reason why we needed this census\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Not that they lack men - God already covered that, <b>he's gonna fight for them</b></li><li class=\"d1\">\"they could bring five guys and they'd still win\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Point = every family its <b>equal share</b>, equal starting point</li><li class=\"d0\">Per Torah, true of <b>everyone on earth</b>, not just Israel</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>Deuteronomy</b> opening: Israel's neighbors</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>St. Paul</b> appeals to it in <b>Acts 17</b></li><li class=\"d0\">God gives each nation and each person a <b>share of what he created</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Can squander it, be lazy, suffer consequences - but <b>not generational</b></li><li class=\"d0\">\"Everyone have an equal opportunity\" - then it's up to you what you do with it</li></ul>"},{"t":1548.3,"lv":3,"h":"Israel strays: Sadducees own the land","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Israel strays far - <b>never do the Sabbath year</b>, let alone Jubilee</li><li class=\"d0\">By <b>Christ's ministry</b>: <b>high priest's family and Sadducees</b> own <b>70%</b> of Judean land not owned by Romans</li><li class=\"d1\">another big chunk owned by <b>Herod</b>; none by the people</li><li class=\"d0\">High priest's family did it on purpose</li><li class=\"d1\">used the <b>temple tax</b> to indebt the people, <b>seize their land</b></li><li class=\"d1\">employed them at low wages on land <b>God gave them to be their own</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Doesn't even approximate what God intended - seen by the Torah as <b>basic injustice</b></li></ul>"},{"t":1618.55,"lv":2,"h":"Numbers 26:57-62 - Levi","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>Levites</b> - no land: they surround the <b>tabernacle</b>, later the <b>temple</b></li><li class=\"d1\">live there, don't farm, serve as priests</li><li class=\"d1\">eat from the <b>offerings</b> others bring</li><li class=\"d0\">Clans: <b>Gershon, Kohath, Merari</b> (Libnites, Hebronites, Korahites, <b>Mushites</b>)</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Kohath</b> → <b>Amram</b>; wife <b>Jochebed</b>, Levi's daughter, born in Egypt</li><li class=\"d1\">bore <b>Aaron, Moses, Miriam</b> - \"where Moses fits\" in the clans of Levi</li><li class=\"d0\">Aaron → <b>Nadab, Abihu, Eleazar, Ithamar</b>; Nadab + Abihu died offering <b>strange fire</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Census <b>23,000</b> - <b>every male from a month old</b></li><li class=\"d1\">no military, no land allotment → military age irrelevant, \"count all the males, period\"</li></ul>"},{"t":1733.24,"lv":2,"h":"Numbers 26:63-65 - Only Caleb and Joshua remain","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Census of Moses + Eleazar - <b>not a man</b> numbered at <b>Sinai</b> remains</li><li class=\"d0\">Not literally every one: some were <b>kids</b> then; maybe a few very elderly, like <b>Moses</b> himself, now too old</li><li class=\"d0\">\"They shall surely die in the desert\" - left only <b>Caleb</b> and <b>Joshua</b>, the two faithful <b>spies</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Caleb</b> - not just a Canaanite but a <b>Kenizzite</b></li><li class=\"d1\">from a group Israel is going to <b>wipe out</b> - but won't kill Caleb</li><li class=\"d1\">he's now <b>elder of the tribe of Judah</b>, head of a clan</li><li class=\"d1\">counted a <b>son of Judah</b>, no biological relation</li><li class=\"d0\">\"This is why our modern concept of <b>ethnicity</b> is not here\"</li></ul>"},{"t":1852.61,"lv":3,"h":"Q&amp;A: grafting in, ethnicity","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Q: reminds me of being <b>grafted in</b>, the new covenant - connected?</li><li class=\"d0\">A: \"essentially the same\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Evangelical/Protestant <b>meme</b>: OT covenant was <b>ethnic</b>, NT is based on <b>belief</b></li><li class=\"d1\">before even the faith question: it was <b>never ethnic</b> as we think of it</li><li class=\"d0\">Nation <b>Israel</b> existed only a couple centuries - \"America's been around longer\"</li><li class=\"d1\">continuous people, but <b>ethnically diverse</b>, esp. at the start</li><li class=\"d0\">Made sons of the patriarchs by a <b>ritual</b>: men <b>circumcised</b>, eat the <b>Passover</b></li><li class=\"d1\">\"no DNA\", no family trees to see if you're Jewish</li><li class=\"d0\">All through: <b>Ruth the Moabite</b>, David's great-grandma; <b>Rahab</b> into Judah</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Deuteronomy</b> lays out process for <b>women</b> - eat Passover (men, women, children all do)</li><li class=\"d0\">So the <b>church is Israel</b>, same group - another <b>big grafting in</b></li><li class=\"d1\">big grafting began it all; little ones continuous → \"not really a disjunction\"</li></ul>"}]});
